WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.980
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:12.090
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:17.660
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:26.430
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:34.180
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.640
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.510
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:44.250
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.920
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.600
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.600 --> 00:01:01.660
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:04.640
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:12.280
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:17.190
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:22.420
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:32.530
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:37.270
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:42.010
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:58.120
What are you talking about?
This is all your fault.

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:00.820
My life has been horrible
ever since you got involved.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:03.520
You butt in on things by yourself,

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:06.160
which keeps me from doing anything!

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:09.130
You're nothing more
than a helpless child.

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:11.700
You're the one who's making me suffer!

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.270
Stop getting in my way!

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:15.940
Now matter how hard you try,

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:18.540
you will never be Kiyotaka Narumi.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:22.780
<i>You'll never be Kiyotaka-san!</i>

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.650
<i>Even so, I have no choice!</i>

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:25.910
<i>"The Man in the High Castle"
Even so, I have no choice!</i>

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:29.680
"The Man in the High Castle"

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:41.460
Well, let's go.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:44.490
What have you done with her?

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:48.190
This train will take you to her.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:51.190
Seems I have no choice.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:55.640
<i>Obey destiny and get on, Ayumu-kun.</i>

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:57.700
Just as you have done thus far.

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:08.680
<i>What's he planning?</i>

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:18.350
<i>There definitely has
to be some sort of trick.</i>

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.580
<i>Where is he sending me?</i>

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:42.920
<i>This is typical of me.</i>

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:44.350
<i>I'm completely helpless,</i>

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:47.950
<i>and I simply let myself be
carried along the tracks...</i>

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.200
Well? How does it feel going on a trip

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.700
all by yourself to
an unknown destination?

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:59.860
Stop playing around.
Tell me what the deal is.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.940
You seem rather annoyed.

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:07.440
Shall I guess what
it is you're thinking?

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:11.310
It's everyone else's fault
that things happen.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:15.090
You simply get caught up in it all,

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:17.520
despite wanting no part of it.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:21.120
That's how you blame
fate on other people.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:22.890
So what?

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:26.700
Your very existence is unpleasant.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.230
Whatever.

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.100
Your attitude, too.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.440
I take it that you haven't
noticed the bomb

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:34.530
I planted on the train yet?

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:38.710
You may be their "hope",

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:42.110
but your actions bring
danger to those around you.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.780
<i>A bomb...</i>

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:52.950
<i>Where?</i>

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.450
<i>Where would he put a bomb?!</i>

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:13.170
-How nice of him to give you that!
-Yeah!

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:23.290
What do you think you're doing?!

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:31.890
Here.

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:37.020
-What is that?
-A rice ball!

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:48.310
Damn...

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:55.090
Have you finally found
little ol' Aril?

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:57.090
Thanks to you.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:59.420
It's too early to breathe easy.

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:00.960
The device is simple.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:05.500
Just enter the password
and the bomb will disarm.

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:08.230
But if you can't enter it,
then it will explode

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:10.830
when you arrive at the next station.

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:13.400
Oh yes, the train windows don't open.

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:16.410
Don't bother trying
to throw it outside.

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:18.780
What are you thinking?

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:21.680
Are you trying to get
innocent people involved?

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:25.410
Of course not. You wouldn't
let that happen, would you?

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:28.920
Just like Rio and the others,

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:31.620
I will give you a chance at victory

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:34.090
in accordance with Kiyotaka's rule.

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:37.560
Will the rainbow gates of Heaven

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:41.430
<i>be where you and Madoka-san reunite?</i>

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:45.330
You have one chance,
mess up and you explode.

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:48.640
What are you thinking?!

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.940
Planting bombs on public vehicles?

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:53.510
You're insane!

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.750
<i>If Kiyotaka was right,
then Ayumu-kun will easily</i>

00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:00.010
be able to overcome
a danger of this size.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:02.750
<i>If Kiyotaka-san was right?</i>

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:06.780
Well, whatever...

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:12.160
I feel sorry for troubling you.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:16.200
<i>But this is the only way
to make Ayumu-kun serious.</i>

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.540
What are you expecting from him?!

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.770
I'm not expecting anything.

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:24.400
I'm simply nipping an
undeveloped bud of hope.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:30.010
<i>Is that you, Narumi-san?</i>

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.110
Can I ask you a favor?

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:35.350
Yes, of course!

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:38.150
I don't mean to brag,
but I've never once said no

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:40.960
to any of your requests!

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.890
Sorry for being so sudden,

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:45.130
but could you tell me
how long it takes to go

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:48.670
from Asahi Wharf
to Seaside Park Station?

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:50.390
Just a second!

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:55.240
Four minutes!

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.440
Though it would be
less than four minutes

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:00.100
if you're on your way
there right now...

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:03.750
Did something happen?

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:07.180
Sorry. I'll explain later.

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:10.650
Understood. I'll wait for
you to contact me again.

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:13.520
Thank you. I owe you one.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:15.830
<i>-Narumi-san!
-What?</i>

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:18.850
If there's anything at all I can do...

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:21.870
In that case, sing a song...

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:24.670
-Eh? A song?
-That weird one.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.830
What's so weird about it?!

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:33.970
<i>Good luck, Narumi-san!</i>

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:41.220
My time limit is 3 minutes...

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:44.890
<i>Think...What's the password?</i>

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:48.160
<i>Will the rainbow gates of Heaven</i>

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.630
<i>be where you and Madoka-san reunite?</i>

00:08:56.670 --> 00:09:00.000
<i>Aril...Rainbow...</i>

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:05.410
<i>Ayumu-kun must be grappling with
the password right about now</i>

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:08.340
<i>Rainbow colors...Aril...</i>

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:10.050
Judging from how he is,

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:13.080
he'll soon realize it's not a color.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:15.390
<i>No, it's not a color.</i>

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:16.780
<i>Then what is it?</i>

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:21.560
<i>Aril...</i>

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:24.320
Do you know what an aril is?

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:28.700
<i>Aril...The flower?</i>

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:33.070
Arils and rainbow gates
share a commonality.

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:34.500
A commonality?

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:36.740
That's it!

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:42.140
The Greek goddess of rainbows.

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:45.350
<i>Iris!</i>

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:48.120
The aril iris and Iris
the rainbow goddess...

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:51.050
Both are written "I-R-I-S".

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:56.790
<i>Now arriving at Seaside Park Station.</i>

00:09:56.790 --> 00:09:59.500
<i>Exits are on the right side.</i>

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:00.620
It's time.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:16.010
<i>Looks like you cleared it, Ayumu-kun.</i>

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:17.910
Though you don't need applause

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:20.180
for stopping something this simple.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:21.380
Where is Madoka?

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:23.610
<i>Get off the train, Ayumu-kun.</i>

00:10:26.420 --> 00:10:28.450
Can you see her?

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:34.560
The boat's about to leave.

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:55.580
<i>It's moving because of inertia...</i>

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:02.660
Another iris...

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:07.060
Now what?

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:09.700
<i>Do you feel like playing now,
Ayumu-kun?</i>

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:11.390
I don't have a choice, do I?

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:14.200
State your business.

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:17.640
<i>That's it, Ayumu-kun.
That's the spirit.</i>

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:20.740
There's a little device
on that boat too.

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:23.180
A bit fancier than the previous one.

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:25.850
Another bomb?

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:27.880
Jump into the ocean and you'll live.

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:31.420
But I won't make it to Madoka.

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:33.160
That's right.

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:34.860
If you can make it past the trap

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:38.290
then the boat will take you to her.

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:42.670
As proof that the boat won't
simply take you to Hell,

00:11:42.670 --> 00:11:44.830
I'll give you a chance to survive.

00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:46.270
<i>Ayumu-kun...</i>

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:50.140
Something besides you
there that has life...

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:51.870
That's your hint.

00:11:55.010 --> 00:11:56.410
<i>Birds?</i>

00:11:56.410 --> 00:12:00.720
You have about two minutes left.

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:03.280
Take too long and it's "the end".

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:19.400
Stop it this instant!

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:22.270
What's the point in doing this?!

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:24.470
What's your goal?!

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:26.910
Point? Goal?

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:29.040
I don't need you telling me
how to do things.

00:12:30.710 --> 00:12:33.480
I'll tell you something
interesting, though...

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:35.580
What you wanted to know...

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:41.780
The place where Kiyotaka Narumi's
favorite irises bloom.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:45.530
Happy, aren't you?

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:50.700
After all, your goal
is always Kiyotaka.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:53.670
<i>Even now, when Ayumu-kun
is on the brink of death.</i>

00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:58.010
But the truth is,
only you can see yourself.

00:12:58.010 --> 00:13:02.170
Your head is filled with more things
about yourself than anyone else.

00:13:03.810 --> 00:13:06.150
Well? Am I wrong?

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:08.920
<i>Birds...</i>

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:13.620
<i>And this iris.</i>

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:15.590
<i>Birds...Irises...</i>

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:19.360
<i>-What?
-Narumi-san?</i>

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:20.460
Oh, it's you.

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:23.770
Sorry, I called because
I was worried about you.

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:25.700
Sorry, but I'm busy right now.

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:27.840
Let me help you!

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:29.940
-Birds...
-Birds?

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:31.810
And irises...

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:33.740
Have you ever heard of an iris-bird?

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:36.480
Isn't that another name for a cuckoo?

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:37.550
Yeah.

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:39.650
Did you know?

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:42.990
Cuckoos are born
in other birds' nests,

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:46.760
and then kick other hatchlings
out so only they survive.

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:47.590
From the moment they're born,

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:50.190
they're destined for
death and destruction...

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:54.360
They bear a cursed fate
and chirp with sadness.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:57.460
What's that have
to do with anything?!

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:05.510
What kind of chirp does
a cuckoo make again?

00:14:05.510 --> 00:14:07.780
Don't they sort of hum?

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:09.710
Hum?!

00:14:09.710 --> 00:14:12.780
Humming! That's it!
That's the truth!

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:14.150
<i>Narumi-san?</i>

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:20.020
The melody of logic
always plays the truth!

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:23.390
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:14:23.390 --> 00:14:27.560
What on a boat hums on and off?

00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:32.600
The engine!

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:45.080
Come on, hum!

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:58.290
<i>I've cleared the bomb for now, but...</i>

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:03.970
On the verge of death,
cuckoos fly about wildly

00:15:03.970 --> 00:15:07.270
before bringing an end
to their own lives.

00:15:07.270 --> 00:15:09.360
Are you still planning something?!

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:17.880
<i>The engine's been rigged...</i>

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:21.010
<i>But now I should be able
to get to Madoka!</i>

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.390
<i>It's going to collide!</i>

00:15:44.970 --> 00:15:46.570
It's sink or swim!

00:16:07.530 --> 00:16:09.170
<i>Welcome, Ayumu-kun.</i>

00:16:09.170 --> 00:16:12.600
<i>Your beloved is in the
warehouse before you.</i>

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:31.850
<i>What kind of factory is this?</i>

00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:51.540
<i>Up here, Ayumu-kun.</i>

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:03.570
Where's Madoka?

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:09.250
She's in the room back there.

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:17.430
<i>Well, Ayumu-kun?</i>

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:21.430
Will you be the princess's
knight in shining armor?

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:38.850
<i>Static electricity?</i>

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:41.090
This is a fireworks factory.

00:17:41.090 --> 00:17:44.220
<i>Even the slightest spark
will prove deadly, Ayumu-kun.</i>

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:46.660
The most frightening fireworks

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:48.530
are the ones that stay on the ground.

00:17:49.970 --> 00:17:51.370
<i>What now?</i>

00:17:51.370 --> 00:17:53.770
<i>Wait, if this is a fireworks factory,</i>

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:55.630
<i>there should be a ground connection...</i>

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:04.780
<i>Oh no!</i>

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:09.690
<i>This is insane...</i>

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:12.620
<i>He's barely giving me
any room to dodge!</i>

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:15.660
<i>Those were less than a centimeter off!</i>

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:17.960
<i>If he keeps throwing
those knives at me,</i>

00:18:17.960 --> 00:18:20.860
<i>my static electricity will
eventually cause an explosion.</i>

00:18:20.860 --> 00:18:23.800
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:25.990
<i>That's it! My synthetic fibers!</i>

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:34.870
Oh, crap!

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:39.220
<i>You should know better, Ayumu-kun.</i>

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:44.690
Static electricity is not that
easily removed from the body.

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:49.150
In other words, I'll cause
a huge explosion myself?

00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:52.730
<i>I've been manipulated...</i>

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:55.500
<i>This is a minefield of explosives!</i>

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:57.470
I assume you've realized?

00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:59.400
As long as you're down there,

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:01.400
you must fear even
the tiniest of sparks

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:04.840
that occur when these knives touch you.

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:07.680
<i>But the static electricity
is just a ploy...</i>

00:19:07.680 --> 00:19:09.710
<i>The real trap is...</i>

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:11.680
You seem to have noticed.

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:17.750
Yes, if you don't save her,
your beloved woman

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:20.860
will be launched together
with the load of fireworks

00:19:20.860 --> 00:19:23.260
and become a star in the night sky...

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:27.250
Of course, it's up to you
if you want to run away.

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:33.360
Courageous, aren't we?

00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:46.980
Madoka...

00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:50.150
When he stands at those crossroads,

00:19:50.150 --> 00:19:52.520
extend a gentle hand to him.

00:19:54.620 --> 00:19:57.790
<i>I'm sorry, Kiyotaka-san...</i>

00:19:57.790 --> 00:19:59.730
<i>I'm sorry, Ayumu...</i>

00:19:59.730 --> 00:20:02.860
<i>I'm...</i>

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:07.060
<i>I'm a useless woman...</i>

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:10.800
<i>So what will it be, Ayumu-kun?</i>

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:16.210
This is the detonator for the bomb

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:18.450
I planted on that lift car.

00:20:18.450 --> 00:20:22.180
In other words,
I can drive you two to death

00:20:22.180 --> 00:20:24.850
with one hand tied behind my back.

00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:27.720
Doing that would put you in danger too!

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:30.390
You needn't worry about me.

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:36.800
You should think about how
to save yourselves instead.

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:38.700
There's no way out...

00:20:39.940 --> 00:20:42.700
You are always powerless
to do anything.

00:20:44.870 --> 00:20:46.710
<i>What will you do, Ayumu-kun?</i>

00:20:46.710 --> 00:20:49.040
You have three choices.

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:51.050
An explosion caused by my bomb,

00:20:51.050 --> 00:20:53.420
an explosion caused
by static electricity,

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:54.820
or...

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:59.250
...complete surrender to me...

00:21:05.890 --> 00:21:11.590
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:11.590 --> 00:21:18.290
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:36.450
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:36.450 --> 00:21:42.090
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:48.000
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:54.570
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:54.570 --> 00:22:00.310
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:22:00.310 --> 00:22:05.510
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:05.510 --> 00:22:11.350
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:22.960
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:28.740
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:35.040
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:39.070 --> 00:22:42.070
Time for Hiyono's Last Episode
Useful News Report Special!

00:22:42.070 --> 00:22:43.770
At the ends of fighting,
will there be salvation?

00:22:43.770 --> 00:22:46.140
Will happiness come
to those who believe?

00:22:46.140 --> 00:22:48.340
The prudent traps,
the shocking suspense...

00:22:48.340 --> 00:22:50.480
The Redemption for life and
the thirst for death will mingle...

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:53.280
What will the sudden conclusion be?!

00:22:53.280 --> 00:22:56.280
On the moving final episode of Spiral:
Bond of Reasoning...

00:22:56.280 --> 00:22:57.790
The Sound of an Iris
Freezing and Melting

00:22:57.790 --> 00:22:59.090
Fate can't be changed...

00:22:59.090 --> 00:23:01.890
No, if you don't try to change it,
then nothing will ever change!

00:23:01.890 --> 00:23:05.990
This has been the final
Hiyono's Playhouse!
